<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35216" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδῐάω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνδιος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stay in the open air</i>:
			generally, <i>linger in</i> or <i>haunt</i> a place, c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάτοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.291.6
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθα δ᾽ ἀνὴρ . . ἐνδιάασκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					22.44
				</span></i>
			: also c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάγους καὶ πρῶνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					3.315
				</span></i>
			: abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ σπήλυγγας</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				4.81
			</span></i>: metaph., [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμμασιν</span>] 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλπὶς ἐνδιάει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.269.10
				</span></i>
			 (Paul. Sil.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. εἰς κενεὰς
				εἰκόνας</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4.4.10
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>):—abs. in 
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκτῖνες ἐνδιάονται</span>
			<i>are bright as day</i> (of the moon), <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				32.6
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδιῶνται:
			μεσημβριάζουσι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιμένες μῆλα ἐνδιάασκον</span> shepherds
				<i>drove</i> their sheep <i>afield</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				16.38
			</span></i> (s. v. l.).</div>
